Order details are submitted.
Food court receives the order.
Staff accepts or rejects it.
Student receives order status.
A similar automated approval process can be designed using AEM workflows.
Note: Your actual food-ordering application would generally implement order processing through its application services, rather than requiring an AEM workflow.
6. Important AEM Workflow Concepts
Workflow Launcher: Starts a workflow automatically when configured conditions are met.
Workflow Participant: User responsible for completing a task.
Workflow Payload: Data or resource on which the workflow operates.
Workflow Instance: An individual execution of a workflow.
Workflow Inbox: Place where users can see and manage assigned tasks.
